// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/deposit_tiers.t27 -- the published security-deposit tiers of the TurboBaby fleet
; Written contract for every surface that shows a deposit: the tier is looked up on the family
; key and no surface computes one. Measured from data/fleet_seed.json (measured_at 2026-09-12),
; whose deposit authority is the published tariff source KB_faq, section "Exact price list
; (from CRM)". Closes issue #18. ASCII only (L3), English identifiers only.
; --
; WHAT READS THIS FILE TODAY: no surface reads its VALUES -- but the absence this paragraph
; used to assert was WIDER than the truth, and it has been narrowed to what can be measured
; (re-measured 2026-09-21). It said: a grep for ".t27" and for "specs/turbobaby" across *.rs,
; *.toml, *.py, *.sh, .github/ and Makefile returns no hit. That grep now returns SIX files --
; scripts/verify_fleet_seed.py, scripts/verify_t27_specs.py, src/trios/market.rs,
; src/trios/pricing.rs, tests/market_clock_wiring.rs and .github/workflows/ci.yml. Exactly one
; of the six names THIS file: scripts/verify_t27_specs.py at :119-121, and what it pins there is
; the module name and the ID, never a deposit. The other five name turbobaby/market and
; turbobaby/pricing-honesty. So the corrected claim is narrower and is still the one that
; matters: this corpus is wired to a COMPILER GATE and not to a consumer, and no shipped surface
; reads FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB. A reader who took the old sentence at face value would have
; concluded that no .t27 is wired to anything, which stopped being true without this file
; noticing. (Re-measured 2026-09-22, and stale again within the day: the same grep returns 19
; files, three of which name THIS file and all three of which are gates, two of them reading a
; deposit. WIRING_REMEASURED_NOTE below has the list; still no shipped surface.) The catalog
; screen renders deposit_thb as it arrives from the API (the field at
; src/ui/screens/catalog_screen.rs:123 rendered through money_thb at :821 (:822 until 2026-09-26) -- :124 and :834 until
; the 2026-09-24 availability edit -- and the field at src/ui/components/bike_card.rs:115 rendered
; through thb_or_dash at :203 (:107 and :195 before the 2026-09-21 published_money edit); all four
; addresses re-verified 2026-09-24, and both pairs had drifted from the :126 and :102 this
; paragraph used to give), and the API is seeded by migrations/082_bikes_seed.sql.
; FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB below is therefore a THIRD copy of the deposit column -- after
; data/fleet_seed.json and migrations/082_bikes_seed.sql -- and a copy is a drift risk (D15).
; It is here because none of the arithmetic below can be checked without it, and the copy is
; STILL ungated -- for a narrower reason than this paragraph used to give (re-verified
; 2026-09-21). It said scripts/verify_fleet_seed.py pins the SQL to the JSON and nothing else,
; that its own docstring says so, and that it knows nothing about .t27. The first clause holds
; exactly, and the deposit column is covered by it: the script parses deposit out of the SQL at
; :48 and compares it with the JSON's deposit_thb at :231. The docstring does still say only
; that (lines 2-19 describe the SQL-to-JSON comparison alone) -- which now makes the docstring
; out of date rather than evidence. The third clause is FALSE: the script binds MARKET_SPEC to
; specs/turbobaby/market_profile.t27 at :34 and compares the seed's market block against that
; contract's constants at :98-140. It gates one spec and this is not it, and the checkable form
; of that is narrow: the string deposit_tier does not occur in the script at all. So comparing
; THIS table to the seed is still the next gate to write -- and the precedent for writing it
; now exists in the same script. The sibling disclosure is corrected with it: availability.t27
; does declare the same gap for its own fleet table, and rental_terms.t27 does NOT -- it holds
; no second copy to gate and says so in its own words at :116, "declares no second copy of that
; algebra". An undeclared third copy
; of a money column is exactly the defect D15 names, so it is declared here.
; Re-measured 2026-09-22: still ungated as a TABLE. scripts/verify_t27_against_source.py now binds
; TIER_2_THB and TIER_3_THB to the xmax-300 and xmax-300-new rows of migrations/082_bikes_seed.sql,
; and the executed asserts tie deposit_thb_of_family on those two keys to FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[6] and
; [7], so two of its fourteen entries are held to their own seed rows through that chain. The COUNT
; of absent entries is held to the seed as well: the same script binds
; FAMILIES_WITHOUT_PUBLISHED_DEPOSIT to the NULL-deposit family rows of that migration, and an
; executed assert recounts it from FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB through families_on_tier(TIER_NONE) -- though
; no gate ties entry [0] to click-125's own row. No other entry is compared with its own row: [2],
; [4] and [8] carry the amounts of the two bound rungs, and equal amounts are not the same rows. The
; table as a whole is not compared.
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-12): the deposit is the sixth heaviest topic in the dialog history the
; tariff was derived from -- 375 client messages -- and issue #18 asked for
; deposit_for(engine_cc, class) over three tiers of 3000 / 5000 / 10000-20000. The seed refutes
; the request in both halves, so this spec does not implement it. Both refutations are recorded
; here rather than in a review comment, because the wrong shape is the cheaper one to write.
; --
; (a) NO SUCH FUNCTION EXISTS. xmax-300 and xmax-300-new are both class "scooter" and both
;     displacement_cc 300, and they carry deposit_thb 5000 and 7000. A function of
;     (class, displacement_cc) would have to return two values for one argument pair. The seed
;     says of the second: "A distinct product from xmax-300, not a trim of it: different
;     tariff, different deposit." The deposit is therefore a PER-FAMILY published attribute
;     with a lookup keyed on the family key, the one column that is unique per row. The field
;     is also named displacement_cc, not engine_cc; the issue misnames it.
; (b) THE TIERS ARE SIX, NOT THREE. The distinct published deposits are 3000, 5000, 7000,
;     15000, 20000 and 25000 baht. 10000 occurs in none of the 21 published rows (14 families
;     in stock, 7 tariff-only), so the issue's top band begins at a number nobody publishes.
;     Its other two bands fail too: scooters carry 3000, 5000, 7000 AND 25000 (KB_faq classes
;     the 750cc X-ADV with the scooters), and 300 cc carries 5000, 7000 AND 15000.
; --
; Totality and non-overlap are therefore stated over the FAMILY-KEY domain -- every offered
; family maps to exactly one of the six tiers -- and not over a displacement band that does not
; exist. A spec asserting a false functional dependency is worse than no spec: the function
; compiles, its tests pass on whichever rows the author happened to pick, and the first
; xmax-300-new booking quoted through it under-collects by 7000 - 5000 = 2000 baht.
; --
; WHAT THIS SPEC NEVER DOES. It never publishes an individual deposit from a past rental (D14):
; the array of them is declared with length zero and must stay that way -- only the aggregate
; tier is public, never a renter's transaction. It never renders an absent deposit as 0:
; click-125 publishes none, D9 makes absent a dash, so the lookup answers a negative marker
; that cannot be read as money. It never computes a client price: no discount is applied to a
; deposit (the 25% / 15% class discounts are RATE discounts), and a rental price comes from the
; door, never from this file (D11). It never says a family is available: the seven tariff-only
; families have published deposits and zero units, and they appear below only as evidence that
; the set of six tiers is closed over them.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module deposit-tiers;

pub const KIND : str = "contract";
pub const ID : str = "turbobaby/deposit-tiers";
pub const NAME : str = "TurboBaby deposit tiers";
; Current t27c does not support brace imports. This names the owner of fleet availability;
; this contract validates only the lengths and totals of its own deposit tables.
pub const REUSES_AVAILABILITY_ID : str = "turbobaby/availability";
pub const SEED : str = "data/fleet_seed.json";
pub const MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-12";
pub const DEPOSIT_AUTHORITY : str = "KB_faq, section 'Exact price list (from CRM)'";
pub const CURRENCY : str = "THB";

; --- The wiring absence, re-measured and pinned as a number ------------------------------
; The header used to assert that NOTHING outside specs/ names a .t27 at all. That absence had
; stopped being true and the sentence went on asserting it, which is the one failure mode a
; reader never checks. The live numbers are kept here so the next drift shows up as a failing
; assert rather than as confident prose. Measured 2026-09-21.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-22: that promise could not be kept, and the numbers below are re-measured.
; Each assert on them compares a constant with a literal, so a drift in the TREE never fails one;
; only an edit to this file can. The grep went from 6 files at 32ebe5c to 8 at f4d84a1 and 19 at
; 2c21df1, all on 2026-09-21 and with every assert here green -- and 2c21df1 edited this very file.
; These are a DATED READING: re-measure and re-date them, do not trust them as a live check. They
; are also not bound in scripts/verify_t27_against_source.py, on purpose: the scope is six globs
; and a tree binding takes one, and a census of the whole tree bound as a live check would go red
; on every new file that cites a spec. Was 6 and 1 (2026-09-21), now 19 and 3; the old reading is
; kept word for word in WIRING_NOTE and the new one is WIRING_REMEASURED_NOTE.
pub const WIRING_GREP_HITS : u8 = 19;
pub const WIRING_GREP_HITS_NAMING_THIS_FILE : u8 = 3;
pub const WIRING_CONSUMERS_OF_THIS_FILE : u8 = 0;
pub const WIRING_REMEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-22";
pub const WIRING_NOTE : str = "grep for .t27 and specs/turbobaby across *.rs, *.toml, *.py, *.sh, .github/ and Makefile returns six files on 2026-09-21: scripts/verify_fleet_seed.py, scripts/verify_t27_specs.py, src/trios/market.rs, src/trios/pricing.rs, tests/market_clock_wiring.rs, .github/workflows/ci.yml. One of the six names this file -- scripts/verify_t27_specs.py, its SPEC_MANIFEST entry for this file (cited by name since 2026-09-24; the line numbers drifted) -- and it pins the module name and the ID only. Zero of the six read a deposit. The contract-versus-wiring gap is therefore real and narrower than it was stated: this corpus is wired to a compiler gate, not to a consumer.";
pub const WIRING_REMEASURED_NOTE : str = "re-measured 2026-09-22 at a33e500 with the commerce source bindings applied: was 6 files and 1 naming this file on 2026-09-21. The same grep over the same six globs returns 19 files: .github/workflows/ci.yml, scripts/execute_t27_assertions.py, scripts/verify_fleet_seed.py, scripts/verify_t27_against_source.py, scripts/verify_t27_specs.py, src/api/cache.rs, src/notification_queue.rs, src/promo.rs, src/trios/market.rs, src/trios/pricing.rs, src/trios/validation.rs, src/ui/api/types.rs, tests/api_document_pairing.rs, tests/events_money_decision_wiring.rs, tests/market_clock_wiring.rs, tests/notification_drain_wiring.rs, tests/promo_copy_wiring.rs, tests/t27_gates_run.rs, tests/wire_absence_wiring.rs. Three name this file and all three are gates. scripts/verify_t27_specs.py pins its module name, its ID, a declaration floor and a check floor -- the floors were already there at 32ebe5c, so the old note's module name and the ID only was narrower than that file. scripts/execute_t27_assertions.py executes every assert here, FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB included, and lists three of its functions as measured front-end disagreements. scripts/verify_t27_against_source.py binds TIER_2_THB, TIER_3_THB, NOT_OFFERED_KEYS and FAMILIES_WITHOUT_PUBLISHED_DEPOSIT to migrations/082_bikes_seed.sql. So two of the three READ a deposit out of this file, both are gates and neither is a consumer: WIRING_CONSUMERS_OF_THIS_FILE counts shipped consumers and is still 0.";

; --- The six tiers ----------------------------------------------------------------------
; The closed set of tier values measured in the published seed. The sources publish an AMOUNT
; per family and no tier name, so a tier is identified by its amount and by its position on the
; ladder; no grade label is invented here. This is an audit taxonomy, not a transaction allowlist:
; an authoritative positive amount outside the measured ladder is shown and logged, never snapped.
pub const TIER_COUNT : u8 = 6;
pub const TIER_1_THB : i32 = 3000;
pub const TIER_2_THB : i32 = 5000;
pub const TIER_3_THB : i32 = 7000;
pub const TIER_4_THB : i32 = 15000;
pub const TIER_5_THB : i32 = 20000;
pub const TIER_6_THB : i32 = 25000;
pub const TIERS_THB : [6]i32 = [3000, 5000, 7000, 15000, 20000, 25000];

; Ladder geometry, each number derived from the tiers above:
;   gaps  5000-3000=2000, 7000-5000=2000, 15000-7000=8000, 20000-15000=5000, 25000-20000=5000
;   sum   2000+2000+8000+5000+5000 = 22000
;   span  25000-3000 = 22000
; A minimum gap above zero is what makes the tiers non-overlapping: these are point values,
; not ranges, so a strictly increasing ladder means no deposit amount can belong to two tiers.
pub const TIER_GAPS_THB : [5]i32 = [2000, 2000, 8000, 5000, 5000];
pub const TIER_GAP_MIN_THB : i32 = 2000;
pub const TIER_GAP_SUM_THB : i32 = 22000;
pub const TIER_SPAN_THB : i32 = 22000;

; --- Markers, and why they are negative -------------------------------------------------
; D9: absent stays absent. A lookup that answered 0 for a family whose deposit is unpublished
; would render as "no deposit required", which is the exact defect D9 was written against. A
; negative marker cannot be mistaken for an amount of money, and it is not zero.
pub const DEPOSIT_ABSENT : i32 = -1;
pub const DEPOSIT_NOT_IN_FLEET : i32 = -2;
pub const TIER_NONE : u8 = 255;

; --- The family-key domain ---------------------------------------------------------------
; The deposits of the 14 in-stock families, in seed order. Fleet keys/counts remain owned by
; availability; the keyed lookup below pins this table without a second shared declaration.
; click-125 is the only family with no published deposit and the only family not offered (D12).
pub const FAMILIES_WITH_PUBLISHED_DEPOSIT : u8 = 13;
pub const FAMILIES_WITHOUT_PUBLISHED_DEPOSIT : u8 = 1;
pub const NOT_OFFERED_KEYS : [1]str = ["click-125"];
; -1 in position 0 is DEPOSIT_ABSENT: click-125 publishes no deposit, not a deposit of zero.
pub const FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB : [14]i32 = [
  -1, 3000, 7000, 15000, 5000, 15000, 5000, 7000, 7000, 20000, 20000, 20000, 20000, 25000,
];

; How many offered families sit on each tier, in tier order. Measured: 3000 x1 (nmax-155),
; 5000 x2 (forza-300, xmax-300), 7000 x3 (xsr-155, xmax-300-new, adv-350), 15000 x2 (cb-300r,
; mt-03-300), 20000 x4 (ninja-400, cb-650r, cbr-650r, vulcan-s-650), 25000 x1 (xadv-750).
; 1+2+3+2+4+1 = 13, which is every offered family: the histogram partitions the domain.
; --
; A sum is not a check. Its own total is invariant under any permutation
; of the six entries, so [2, 1, 3, 2, 4, 1] -- two families at 3000 and one at 5000, which the
; seed refutes -- would satisfy both and change nothing that fails. families_on_tier() below
; therefore recounts each rung from FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB, which is itself pinned row by row
; against the lookup, and the test compares the recount with each entry of this table.
pub const TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS : [6]u8 = [1, 2, 3, 2, 4, 1];
pub const TIER_FAMILY_COUNT_SUM : u8 = 13;

; --- The refutation, as numbers ----------------------------------------------------------
; The three scooters at 300 cc are forza-300 (5000), xmax-300 (5000) and xmax-300-new (7000):
; three families, two distinct deposits, one (class, displacement_cc) pair. Two distinct values
; at one argument pair is precisely what a function may not have, so the count below is the
; measurement that killed deposit_for(engine_cc, class).
; --
; THE TWO AXES OF THE REFUTATION ARE NOT DECLARED HERE. bike-catalog.t27 owns the class algebra
; (CLASSES, CLASS_SCOOTER, CLASS_MOTORCYCLE, CLASS_COUNT, CLASS_NONE) and the displacement axis
; (DISPLACEMENTS_CC, the count and the three bands); its own header states that no count is
; typed twice. (This sentence used to credit the general form of that rule to discovery.t27.
; There is no such file in this corpus -- find specs -type f returns 43 files, and none of them
; is discovery.t27, measured 2026-09-21 -- so the attribution is withdrawn and the rule is
; stated on its own: no owner, limit or exclusion is typed twice.)
; An earlier draft of this file re-declared CLASSES and DISPLACEMENTS_CC verbatim,
; and the drift that rule exists to prevent had already happened: measured 2026-09-12 the same
; seven displacements were [7]u16 in bike-catalog.t27 and [7]i16 in ride-game.t27, one fact at
; two integer widths. Re-measured 2026-09-21 that particular drift is closed -- turbobaby/bike-
; catalog owns DISPLACEMENTS_CC and turbobaby/ride-game declares DISPLACEMENTS_CC under the same
; name, and both are now pub const DISPLACEMENTS_CC : [7]u16 with identical elements
; -- and the sentence is kept in the past tense rather than deleted, because
; the reason this file carries no copy is the drift being POSSIBLE, not the drift being present.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-24: turbobaby/ride-game no longer declares DISPLACEMENTS_CC at all. It names
; turbobaby/bike-catalog as the owner of the displacement domain and takes a displacement as a bare
; argument, so the second declaration measured above is gone and only the owner's remains. A file whose whole argument is that displacement and class are NOT its
; axis has no business carrying one more copy of either, so both are gone. The class of a family
; is read from the seed's class column (families[13].class == "scooter" for xadv-750) and cited
; in prose where it is needed; the displacement of a family is carried by the family key itself
; ("xadv-750"), which is the one column this spec is keyed on.
pub const SCOOTER_300CC_FAMILIES : u8 = 3;
pub const SCOOTER_300CC_DISTINCT_DEPOSITS : u8 = 2;
; Occurrences of the issue's 10000 tier across all 21 published rows -- recounted from the two
; tables in this file by published_rows_at_amount(), not asserted against itself.
pub const DEPOSIT_10000_OCCURRENCES : u8 = 0;

; --- Published in the tariff, zero units in the fleet ------------------------------------
; Listed so that a reader who finds a tariff without stock does not invent the stock. Their
; deposits are all drawn from the same six tiers, which is the evidence that the set is closed
; rather than merely enumerated from the 14 in-stock rows. They must never read as available,
; and deposit_thb_of_family() deliberately does not answer for them.
; RESOLVED 2026-09-24: HOW MANY UNITS these families have is not this file's fact. A unit count is
; fleet availability, and turbobaby/availability (REUSES_AVAILABILITY_ID above) declares this one as
; PRICE_LIST_ONLY_UNITS, 0, beside PRICE_LIST_ONLY_FAMILIES. This file declared the same zero under
; the same name until this edit, although its own header says it validates only the lengths and
; totals of its own deposit tables; a review of 2026-09-23 recorded the pair as a restated fact
; with no gate reading both sides. The copy is dropped, not pinned. What it stood for here -- these
; rows never read as available -- is carried by deposit_thb_of_family refusing them
; (DEPOSIT_NOT_IN_FLEET), and the count itself is consumed from the owner by name.
pub const PRICE_LIST_ONLY_UNIT_COUNT_IS_DECLARED_HERE : bool = false;
pub const AVAILABILITY_UNIT_COUNT_DECLARATION : str = "PRICE_LIST_ONLY_UNITS";
pub const RESTATEMENT_DROPPED_ON_RESOLUTION : [1]str = ["PRICE_LIST_ONLY_UNITS"];
pub const RESTATEMENT_RESOLVED_AT : str = "2026-09-24";
pub const PRICE_LIST_ONLY_KEYS : [7]str = [
  "pcx-150", "adv-150", "pcx-160", "adv-160", "rebel-300", "xsr-900", "r7",
];
pub const PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB : [7]i32 = [3000, 3000, 5000, 5000, 15000, 20000, 25000];

; --- D14: the aggregate tier is public, the transaction is not ---------------------------
; The rental-history sheet holds what each renter paid and what was returned. None of it is
; here, and the empty array is the structural form of that prohibition: a later worker who
; wants to add one has to change a declared length, which cannot pass as a tidy-up.
pub const PAST_RENTAL_DEPOSITS_THB : [0]i32 = [];
pub const PAST_RENTAL_DEPOSIT_RULE : str = "Only the aggregate per-family tier is public. No deposit taken from or returned to an individual renter enters this repository in any form.";

; --- The form of the deposit: money OR the passport, never both --------------------------
; Quoted from rental_terms.deposit in the seed, byte for byte: DEPOSIT_FORM_RULE is
; rental_terms.deposit.rule, DEPOSIT_MONEY_METHODS is the first three entries of
; rental_terms.deposit.accepted, and DEPOSIT_FOREIGN_CURRENCY_RULE is
; rental_terms.deposit.foreign_currency. They must diff clean against the JSON; a reworded
; string under a comment that calls itself a quotation is a false provenance claim, and the
; next reader cannot tell which of the two texts governs.
; --
; The accepted list holds four entries, of which three are ways of paying money and the fourth
; is "passport in place of money" -- so there are two FORMS, not four, and taking both at once
; is not a stricter policy but a different one. DEPOSIT_FORMS is this file's own naming of those
; two forms and is not presented as a quotation: the seed names no form at all.
pub const DEPOSIT_FORMS : [2]str = ["money", "passport"];
pub const DEPOSIT_FORM_LEGAL_STATES : u8 = 2;
pub const DEPOSIT_FORM_RULE : str = "Deposit is EITHER money OR the passport - never both.";
pub const DEPOSIT_MONEY_METHODS : [3]str = ["cash THB", "bank transfer", "USDT"];
pub const DEPOSIT_FOREIGN_CURRENCY_RULE : str = "Take the model's THB deposit, convert to an approximate USD/EUR equivalent, round to hundreds. Return by the same method and at the same fixed amount that was agreed.";
; The class and term discounts are RATE discounts. A deposit is quoted at its tier, undiscounted.
pub const DEPOSIT_DISCOUNT_APPLIES : bool = false;

; --- The agreed refund, made executable (added 2026-09-20) --------------------------------
; WHY (measured 2026-09-20): docs/t27-semantic-merge-matrix.md:62 records the root spec's
; ":201-257 payment methods, unpublished FX conversion, hundred rounding and fixed refund" as
; two different things -- the public policy, MERGED into DEPOSIT_FOREIGN_CURRENCY_RULE above,
; and an executable FX/refund state left as a DEFERRED follow-up "for the commerce runtime".
; The two halves of that row are no longer in the same condition, and keeping them bundled
; keeps the dischargeable half deferred by association.
;   (a) FX STAYS REFUSED. It needs a published rate authority and there is none:
;       turbobaby/market owns EXCHANGE_RATES_PUBLISHED, declared as [0]str = [], and
;       DECISIONS.md:347 states that no exchange rate enters this repository without a source.
;   (b) THE REFUND DOES NOT NEED ONE, and the record it needs already exists. Measured in
;       src/db/orders.rs:551-586: enum DepositForm { Money { amount: Option<f64>,
;       currency: Option<String>, method: Option<String> }, Passport }. Its own doc comment
;       (orders.rs:622-624) says the money "must be returned by the same method and at the
;       same fixed amount that was agreed, which is why the method is recorded next to the
;       figure rather than inferred later", and the Passport variant "carries no amount at
;       all" (orders.rs:653-655). Same method, same currency, same figure is a COMPARISON of
;       three fields that are already written down. No rate is read, so no rate is needed.
; The rule below is therefore CURRENCY-PRESERVING by construction: the two currencies are
; compared and neither is privileged, and no expression anywhere on the money path multiplies,
; scales, rounds or subtracts. That is the whole of what (b) discharges; (a) stays refused, in
; named constants, a few lines down.
; --
; D14 is untouched by the addition. refund_decision() takes the facts of one rental as
; ARGUMENTS and stores none of them; PAST_RENTAL_DEPOSITS_THB stays [0]i32. A refund DECISION
; is a rule, and a refund RECORD would be a renter's transaction, which is still prohibited
; repository data. The tiers are untouched too: a refund returns the figure that was agreed,
; which need not be one of the six rungs -- a foreign-currency deposit is not one of them, and
; an unmatched positive amount is shown and logged rather than snapped (publishable_deposit).
pub const REUSES_MARKET_PROFILE_ID : str = "turbobaby/market";
; The declaration this file leans on, named rather than addressed by line. Three paragraphs
; above used to cite it as market_profile.t27:135, and a line number into a sibling is stale the
; day that sibling is edited; the owner plus the declaration name is not.
pub const MARKET_FX_DECLARATION : str = "EXCHANGE_RATES_PUBLISHED";
pub const REFUND_SOURCE_ENUM : str = "src/db/orders.rs:551-586 enum DepositForm { Money { amount, currency, method }, Passport }";
; This file's own naming of the rule, like DEPOSIT_FORMS above, and NOT presented as a
; quotation: the seed's own sentence is DEPOSIT_FOREIGN_CURRENCY_RULE and stays byte for byte.
pub const REFUND_RULE : str = "A deposit comes back in the form it was taken: the passport as the document and no money at all, money by the method it arrived by, in the currency it was agreed in and at the figure that was agreed. A request that changes the method, the currency or the amount is not a refund this contract authorizes.";

; orders.rs records the currency and the method as Option<String>; None arrives here as the
; empty string, the same way an unknown key does in deposit_thb_of_family(""). It is not a
; method and not a currency, and the money path refuses it instead of guessing one.
pub const DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED : str = "";
; The "no rung" convention of TIER_NONE, reused for the method table: 255 is not an index into
; a three-entry list, so it cannot be mistaken for one.
pub const MONEY_METHOD_NONE : u8 = 255;

; The outcomes of one refund request. Two of them hand something back and seven refuse; the
; two are numbered first, so an outcome below REFUND_AUTHORIZED_OUTCOMES is exactly an
; authorized one. That correspondence is checked code by code below rather than assumed from
; the numbering, because a renumbering that broke it would otherwise pass in silence.
pub const REFUND_RETURN_DOCUMENT : u8 = 0;
pub const REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD : u8 = 1;
pub const REFUND_REFUSED_FORM_ILLEGAL : u8 = 2;
pub const REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_UNRECORDED : u8 = 3;
pub const REFUND_REFUSED_CURRENCY_UNRECORDED : u8 = 4;
pub const REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_UNAGREED : u8 = 5;
pub const REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_CHANGED : u8 = 6;
pub const REFUND_REFUSED_CURRENCY_CHANGED : u8 = 7;
pub const REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_CHANGED : u8 = 8;
pub const REFUND_OUTCOME_COUNT : u8 = 9;
pub const REFUND_AUTHORIZED_OUTCOMES : u8 = 2;

; --- What the refund rule refuses to do, and what would be needed to allow it -------------
; Each of the three would be a NUMBER this file can only invent. They are declared as named
; flags rather than left unwritten, so that a later worker who wants one has to flip a flag
; and name a source, which cannot pass as a tidy-up.
; FX: would need a published exchange-rate authority with a source. There is none --
; turbobaby/market owns EXCHANGE_RATES_PUBLISHED and declares it [0]str = [], and
; DECISIONS.md:347 says why. The
; seed's own sentence puts the conversion at the door, by hand, BEFORE anything is agreed;
; what is agreed is then a fixed figure, and the refund returns that figure.
pub const REFUND_FX_CONVERSION_ALLOWED : bool = false;
; PARTIAL: would need a published deduction schedule -- what a scratch, a late hour or a
; missing litre costs. data/fleet_seed.json:289-293 publishes the rule, the accepted forms and
; the foreign-currency sentence, and no deduction table at all. Without one, a part-refund is
; a number invented at the keyboard, which is the D11 defect with its sign reversed.
pub const REFUND_PARTIAL_AMOUNT_ALLOWED : bool = false;
; FEES: would need a published fee schedule (bank transfer fee, USDT network fee, and which
; side pays it). The seed publishes none, so there is nothing to net off: the agreed figure is
; the figure.
pub const REFUND_FEE_SUBTRACTION_ALLOWED : bool = false;

// ============================================================================
// Lookups
//
// Keyed on the family key, because that is the only key the deposit is a function of.
// ============================================================================

; The published deposit of an in-stock family, in baht.
;   >= 0                   the family's tier
;   DEPOSIT_ABSENT (-1)    the family exists and publishes no deposit (click-125): render a dash
;   DEPOSIT_NOT_IN_FLEET   the key is not one of the 14 in-stock families; this includes the
;                          seven tariff-only keys, which have a published deposit but no unit,
;                          and must not be answered here as though they were rentable
pub fn deposit_thb_of_family(key: str) i32 {
    if (key == "click-125") {
        return DEPOSIT_ABSENT;
    }
    if (key == "nmax-155") {
        return TIER_1_THB;
    }
    if (key == "xsr-155") {
        return TIER_3_THB;
    }
    if (key == "cb-300r") {
        return TIER_4_THB;
    }
    if (key == "forza-300") {
        return TIER_2_THB;
    }
    if (key == "mt-03-300") {
        return TIER_4_THB;
    }
    if (key == "xmax-300") {
        return TIER_2_THB;
    }
    if (key == "xmax-300-new") {
        return TIER_3_THB;
    }
    if (key == "adv-350") {
        return TIER_3_THB;
    }
    if (key == "ninja-400") {
        return TIER_5_THB;
    }
    if (key == "cb-650r") {
        return TIER_5_THB;
    }
    if (key == "cbr-650r") {
        return TIER_5_THB;
    }
    if (key == "vulcan-s-650") {
        return TIER_5_THB;
    }
    if (key == "xadv-750") {
        return TIER_6_THB;
    }
    return DEPOSIT_NOT_IN_FLEET;
}

; Position of an amount on the ladder, or TIER_NONE if the amount is not a published tier.
; This is what makes "exactly one tier" checkable: an amount either matches one rung or none.
pub fn tier_index_of(deposit_thb: i32) u8 {
    if (deposit_thb == TIER_1_THB) {
        return 0;
    }
    if (deposit_thb == TIER_2_THB) {
        return 1;
    }
    if (deposit_thb == TIER_3_THB) {
        return 2;
    }
    if (deposit_thb == TIER_4_THB) {
        return 3;
    }
    if (deposit_thb == TIER_5_THB) {
        return 4;
    }
    if (deposit_thb == TIER_6_THB) {
        return 5;
    }
    return TIER_NONE;
}

pub fn is_published_tier(deposit_thb: i32) bool {
    return tier_index_of(deposit_thb) != TIER_NONE;
}

; Transaction boundary retained from the root contract. A positive authoritative amount is
; publishable even when it is not one of today's six seed tiers; an unmatched value is an audit
; event, not permission to rewrite money. Zero and negatives remain absent/invalid under D9.
pub fn publishable_deposit(deposit_thb: i32) bool {
    return deposit_thb > 0;
}

pub fn deposit_needs_tier_log(deposit_thb: i32) bool {
    return publishable_deposit(deposit_thb) and !is_published_tier(deposit_thb);
}

; How many of the 14 in-stock families sit on one rung, recounted from the family table rather
; than read off TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS. This is what turns the histogram from a restatement into a
; measurement: a permuted table now disagrees with the recount and fails.
; click-125 carries DEPOSIT_ABSENT, whose tier_index_of is TIER_NONE, so it is counted on no
; rung -- and passing TIER_NONE as the argument counts exactly the families with no rung at all.
; The accumulator is u8 because the largest possible answer is 14.
pub fn families_on_tier(tier_index: u8) u8 {
    var found : u8 = 0;
    var i : u8 = 0;
    while (i < 14) : (i += 1) {
        if (tier_index_of(FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[i]) == tier_index) {
            found = found + 1;
        }
    }
    return found;
}

; How many of the 21 published rows -- the 14 in stock plus the 7 tariff-only -- carry one exact
; amount. The 10000 tier the issue asked for is a claim about all 21 rows, and asserting the
; constant DEPOSIT_10000_OCCURRENCES against itself proves nothing about them; this counts.
pub fn published_rows_at_amount(amount_thb: i32) u8 {
    var found : u8 = 0;
    var i : u8 = 0;
    while (i < 14) : (i += 1) {
        if (FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[i] == amount_thb) {
            found = found + 1;
        }
    }
    var j : u8 = 0;
    while (j < 7) : (j += 1) {
        if (PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB[j] == amount_thb) {
            found = found + 1;
        }
    }
    return found;
}

; Exactly one of the two forms is held for the duration of a rental. Both is forbidden by the
; rule; neither means no deposit was taken at all, which is not a rental this shop writes.
pub fn deposit_form_is_legal(money_taken: bool, passport_held: bool) bool {
    if (money_taken == true) {
        if (passport_held == true) {
            return false;
        }
        return true;
    }
    if (passport_held == true) {
        return true;
    }
    return false;
}

; Which of the three accepted money methods this is, or MONEY_METHOD_NONE. The table is
; DEPOSIT_MONEY_METHODS above -- the first three entries of rental_terms.deposit.accepted --
; and is not retyped here. The fourth entry of that seed list, "passport in place of money",
; is a FORM and not a method, so it answers MONEY_METHOD_NONE like anything else that is not
; money; so does "Thai PromptPay QR transfer", which the seed accepts as a PAYMENT method
; (data/fleet_seed.json:294) and not as a deposit (data/fleet_seed.json:291).
pub fn money_method_index_of(method: str) u8 {
    if (method == DEPOSIT_MONEY_METHODS[0]) {
        return 0;
    }
    if (method == DEPOSIT_MONEY_METHODS[1]) {
        return 1;
    }
    if (method == DEPOSIT_MONEY_METHODS[2]) {
        return 2;
    }
    return MONEY_METHOD_NONE;
}

; The refund of one deposit, decided from what was agreed and what is being asked for.
;   money_taken, passport_held   the two form discriminants deposit_form_is_legal() judges
;   agreed_*                     what src/db/orders.rs:551-586 recorded when the bike went out
;   requested_*                  what is being asked for now
; agreed_amount and requested_amount are figures in their own currency -- THB for the six
; published rungs, the door's agreed USD/EUR figure for a foreign-currency deposit -- and this
; function only ever COMPARES them. DEPOSIT_ABSENT stands for the orders.rs amount None, and
; DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED for a currency or method None.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-24 (T27 C3): an order no longer records the door's USD/EUR FIGURE. The
; order path refuses a figure in any currency but THB (turbobaby/commerce
; CLIENT_DEPOSIT_FOREIGN_FIGURE_IS_ADMITTED false, DepositRefusal::NotComparable in
; src/api/orders.rs) until the owner decides how a foreign deposit is recorded; only the money
; form with no figure passes in another currency, so a foreign deposit can reach an order as a
; currency with amount None (DEPOSIT_ABSENT here) and never as a figure. The sentence above is
; kept as written, and this function is unchanged: it still compares whatever it is given.
; --
; Order of the gates, and why it is this order:
;   1. an illegal form pair (both, or neither) is refused before any figure is read at all;
;   2. the passport form is answered next, because it has no method, no currency and no
;      amount, so the money gates have nothing to read on it;
;   3. the money record is checked for COMPLETENESS before it is compared with the request:
;      two unrecorded methods are equal to each other, and comparing first would let an empty
;      record authorize itself. This is the fail-closed gate;
;   4. only then are method, currency and amount compared, one refusal code each.
pub fn refund_decision(money_taken: bool, passport_held: bool, agreed_amount: i32, agreed_currency: str, agreed_method: str, requested_amount: i32, requested_currency: str, requested_method: str) u8 {
    if (!deposit_form_is_legal(money_taken, passport_held)) {
        return REFUND_REFUSED_FORM_ILLEGAL;
    }
    if (passport_held == true) {
        // The document goes back and nothing else moves. A request that names a method, a
        // currency or an amount is asking for something this deposit never was -- buying a
        // held passport out for money is a different transaction, not a refund -- so each of
        // the three is refused by the gate that owns it.
        if (requested_method != DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED) {
            return REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_CHANGED;
        }
        if (requested_currency != DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED) {
            return REFUND_REFUSED_CURRENCY_CHANGED;
        }
        if (requested_amount != DEPOSIT_ABSENT) {
            return REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_CHANGED;
        }
        return REFUND_RETURN_DOCUMENT;
    }
    // Past the form gate and not the passport, so money_taken is true: those are the only two
    // legal states of the pair.
    if (money_method_index_of(agreed_method) == MONEY_METHOD_NONE) {
        return REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_UNRECORDED;
    }
    if (agreed_currency == DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED) {
        return REFUND_REFUSED_CURRENCY_UNRECORDED;
    }
    // publishable_deposit() is reused here for exactly what it is: a sign test on an amount.
    // Its parameter is named for THB because every published rung is in THB, but the test it
    // performs is currency-free and nothing here converts. An amount that is not positive was
    // never agreed -- DEPOSIT_ABSENT is the orders.rs amount None, and 0 is the D9 defect, a
    // figure that reads as "no deposit owed".
    if (!publishable_deposit(agreed_amount)) {
        return REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_UNAGREED;
    }
    if (requested_method != agreed_method) {
        return REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_CHANGED;
    }
    if (requested_currency != agreed_currency) {
        return REFUND_REFUSED_CURRENCY_CHANGED;
    }
    if (requested_amount != agreed_amount) {
        return REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_CHANGED;
    }
    return REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD;
}

pub fn refund_is_authorized(decision: u8) bool {
    return decision == REFUND_RETURN_DOCUMENT or decision == REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD;
}

; True only for the one outcome that moves a figure. The passport outcome is authorized and
; moves nothing, which is why "authorized" and "moves money" are two questions here.
pub fn refund_moves_money(decision: u8) bool {
    return decision == REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD;
}

; The figure a refund hands back. There is no arithmetic operator in this body on purpose: the
; one path that moves money returns the agreed figure UNCHANGED, and every other path returns
; the absent marker. A conversion, a part-refund or a netted fee would each have to appear
; here as arithmetic, and there is nowhere for it to hide.
pub fn refund_amount_returned(decision: u8, agreed_amount: i32) i32 {
    if (decision == REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD) {
        return agreed_amount;
    }
    return DEPOSIT_ABSENT;
}

// ============================================================================
// Tests
//
// The band boundaries the issue asked for, read off the only axis that exists: the tier
// ladder, plus one test per distinct displacement so that the displacements the issue named
// (125, 155, 300, 350, 400, 650, 750) are each exercised -- and so that the two of them which
// carry more than one deposit say so out loud.
//
// Those seven tests do not assert a cc value. The displacement table belongs to
// bike-catalog.t27 and a local copy would be one more of it; each test instead reaches its
// families through the family key, the axis this spec is keyed on, and the key carries the
// displacement in its own name ("nmax-155", "adv-350", "xadv-750"). A test name here states
// only what its body checks -- the deposits of the families at that displacement.
// ============================================================================

test the_six_tiers_are_the_closed_set_measured_in_the_seed {
    assert TIERS_THB.len == TIER_COUNT;
    assert TIERS_THB[0] == TIER_1_THB;
    assert TIERS_THB[1] == TIER_2_THB;
    assert TIERS_THB[2] == TIER_3_THB;
    assert TIERS_THB[3] == TIER_4_THB;
    assert TIERS_THB[4] == TIER_5_THB;
    assert TIERS_THB[5] == TIER_6_THB;
}

test an_unmatched_positive_deposit_is_shown_and_logged_not_snapped {
    assert publishable_deposit(6000) == true;
    assert is_published_tier(6000) == false;
    assert deposit_needs_tier_log(6000) == true;
    assert deposit_needs_tier_log(TIER_3_THB) == false;
    assert publishable_deposit(0) == false;
    assert publishable_deposit(DEPOSIT_ABSENT) == false;
}

test the_tier_the_issue_asked_for_is_published_nowhere {
    assert DEPOSIT_10000_OCCURRENCES == 0;
    assert is_published_tier(10000) == false;
    assert tier_index_of(10000) == TIER_NONE;
    // ...and the constant is the recount of all 21 published rows, not a number typed twice.
    assert published_rows_at_amount(10000) == DEPOSIT_10000_OCCURRENCES;
    assert published_rows_at_amount(10000) == 0;
}

; The 21 published rows, counted by amount: 20 of them carry one of the six tiers and exactly
; one carries no deposit at all. 21 is not typed here -- it is the two published counts, and
; each of those is pinned to the length of its own table elsewhere in this file.
test the_six_rungs_account_for_every_published_row {
    assert published_rows_at_amount(TIER_1_THB) + published_rows_at_amount(TIER_2_THB) + published_rows_at_amount(TIER_3_THB) + published_rows_at_amount(TIER_4_THB) + published_rows_at_amount(TIER_5_THB) + published_rows_at_amount(TIER_6_THB) == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB.len + PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB.len - FAMILIES_WITHOUT_PUBLISHED_DEPOSIT;
    assert published_rows_at_amount(DEPOSIT_ABSENT) == FAMILIES_WITHOUT_PUBLISHED_DEPOSIT;
    assert published_rows_at_amount(0) == 0;
}

test each_rung_of_the_ladder_is_its_own_index {
    assert tier_index_of(TIER_1_THB) == 0;
    assert tier_index_of(TIER_2_THB) == 1;
    assert tier_index_of(TIER_3_THB) == 2;
    assert tier_index_of(TIER_4_THB) == 3;
    assert tier_index_of(TIER_5_THB) == 4;
    assert tier_index_of(TIER_6_THB) == 5;
}

test the_gaps_are_the_differences_of_the_tiers_they_separate {
    assert TIER_GAPS_THB.len == TIER_COUNT - 1;
    assert TIERS_THB[1] - TIERS_THB[0] == TIER_GAPS_THB[0];
    assert TIERS_THB[2] - TIERS_THB[1] == TIER_GAPS_THB[1];
    assert TIERS_THB[3] - TIERS_THB[2] == TIER_GAPS_THB[2];
    assert TIERS_THB[4] - TIERS_THB[3] == TIER_GAPS_THB[3];
    assert TIERS_THB[5] - TIERS_THB[4] == TIER_GAPS_THB[4];
}

test the_pinned_minimum_gap_really_is_the_smallest_one {
    assert TIER_GAP_MIN_THB <= TIER_GAPS_THB[0];
    assert TIER_GAP_MIN_THB <= TIER_GAPS_THB[1];
    assert TIER_GAP_MIN_THB <= TIER_GAPS_THB[2];
    assert TIER_GAP_MIN_THB <= TIER_GAPS_THB[3];
    assert TIER_GAP_MIN_THB <= TIER_GAPS_THB[4];
    assert TIER_GAP_MIN_THB == 2000;
}

test the_gaps_sum_to_the_span_so_no_rung_is_missing {
    assert TIER_GAPS_THB[0] + TIER_GAPS_THB[1] + TIER_GAPS_THB[2] + TIER_GAPS_THB[3] + TIER_GAPS_THB[4] == TIER_GAP_SUM_THB;
    assert TIERS_THB[5] - TIERS_THB[0] == TIER_SPAN_THB;
    assert TIER_GAP_SUM_THB == TIER_SPAN_THB;
}

test the_histogram_counts_every_offered_family_once {
    assert TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS.len == TIER_COUNT;
    assert TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS[0] + TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS[1] + TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS[2] + TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS[3] + TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS[4] + TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS[5] == TIER_FAMILY_COUNT_SUM;
    assert TIER_FAMILY_COUNT_SUM == FAMILIES_WITH_PUBLISHED_DEPOSIT;
    assert FAMILIES_WITH_PUBLISHED_DEPOSIT + FAMILIES_WITHOUT_PUBLISHED_DEPOSIT == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB.len;
}

; The test the sum above cannot be: each rung is recounted from FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB and compared
; with the published entry, so a permutation of TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS fails here even though every
; total still closes. The last two lines close the domain from the other end: one family has no
; rung (click-125, DEPOSIT_ABSENT), and 13 + 1 is the whole fleet.
test each_rung_is_recounted_from_the_family_table {
    assert families_on_tier(0) == TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS[0];
    assert families_on_tier(1) == TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS[1];
    assert families_on_tier(2) == TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS[2];
    assert families_on_tier(3) == TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS[3];
    assert families_on_tier(4) == TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS[4];
    assert families_on_tier(5) == TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS[5];
    assert families_on_tier(TIER_NONE) == FAMILIES_WITHOUT_PUBLISHED_DEPOSIT;
    assert families_on_tier(0) + families_on_tier(1) + families_on_tier(2) + families_on_tier(3) + families_on_tier(4) + families_on_tier(5) + families_on_tier(TIER_NONE) == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB.len;
}

; The table and the lookup are two statements of one fact, so they are checked against each
; other row by row. A drift between them is what this test exists to fail on.
test the_table_and_the_lookup_agree_on_all_fourteen_families {
    assert FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB.len == 14;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("click-125") == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[0];
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("nmax-155") == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[1];
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("xsr-155") == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[2];
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("cb-300r") == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[3];
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("forza-300") == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[4];
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("mt-03-300") == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[5];
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("xmax-300") == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[6];
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("xmax-300-new") == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[7];
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("adv-350") == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[8];
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("ninja-400") == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[9];
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("cb-650r") == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[10];
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("cbr-650r") == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[11];
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("vulcan-s-650") == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[12];
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("xadv-750") == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB[13];
}

; Totality, one family at a time: every offered key lands on a rung, never on TIER_NONE.
test every_offered_family_lands_on_exactly_one_rung {
    assert tier_index_of(deposit_thb_of_family("nmax-155")) == 0;
    assert tier_index_of(deposit_thb_of_family("forza-300")) == 1;
    assert tier_index_of(deposit_thb_of_family("xmax-300")) == 1;
    assert tier_index_of(deposit_thb_of_family("xsr-155")) == 2;
    assert tier_index_of(deposit_thb_of_family("xmax-300-new")) == 2;
    assert tier_index_of(deposit_thb_of_family("adv-350")) == 2;
    assert tier_index_of(deposit_thb_of_family("cb-300r")) == 3;
    assert tier_index_of(deposit_thb_of_family("mt-03-300")) == 3;
    assert tier_index_of(deposit_thb_of_family("ninja-400")) == 4;
    assert tier_index_of(deposit_thb_of_family("cb-650r")) == 4;
    assert tier_index_of(deposit_thb_of_family("cbr-650r")) == 4;
    assert tier_index_of(deposit_thb_of_family("vulcan-s-650")) == 4;
    assert tier_index_of(deposit_thb_of_family("xadv-750")) == 5;
}

; ---- one test per displacement the issue named -----------------------------------------

test at_125cc_the_one_family_publishes_no_deposit_and_is_not_offered {
    assert NOT_OFFERED_KEYS[0] == "click-125";
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("click-125") == DEPOSIT_ABSENT;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("click-125") < 0;
    assert is_published_tier(DEPOSIT_ABSENT) == false;
}

test at_155cc_two_families_carry_two_different_tiers {
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("nmax-155") == 3000;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("xsr-155") == 7000;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("xsr-155") - deposit_thb_of_family("nmax-155") == 4000;
}

test at_300cc_five_families_carry_three_different_tiers {
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("forza-300") == 5000;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("xmax-300") == 5000;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("xmax-300-new") == 7000;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("cb-300r") == 15000;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("mt-03-300") == 15000;
}

test at_350cc_the_one_family_sits_on_the_third_rung {
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("adv-350") == 7000;
    assert tier_index_of(deposit_thb_of_family("adv-350")) == 2;
}

test at_400cc_the_one_family_sits_on_the_fifth_rung {
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("ninja-400") == 20000;
    assert tier_index_of(deposit_thb_of_family("ninja-400")) == 4;
}

test at_650cc_three_families_share_one_tier {
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("cb-650r") == 20000;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("cbr-650r") == 20000;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("vulcan-s-650") == 20000;
}

; The earlier name of this test was "..._is_carried_by_a_scooter" over a body that asserted
; CLASSES[0] == "scooter" -- that the string "scooter" sits at index 0 of a local class table,
; which is true of the table and says nothing about this bike. The seed does class the X-ADV
; with the scooters (families[13].class == "scooter"), and that fact carries the header's
; refutation of the issue's "scooters are the cheap band"; but the class column is owned by
; bike-catalog.t27 and is not tabulated here, so the name now claims only what the body checks:
; exactly one family stands on the top rung, and it is the X-ADV.
test at_750cc_the_top_rung_is_the_xadv_and_only_the_xadv {
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("xadv-750") == 25000;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("xadv-750") == TIER_6_THB;
    assert families_on_tier(5) == 1;
    assert families_on_tier(5) == TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS[5];
}

; ---- the measurement that forced the shape of this spec --------------------------------

test the_xmax_300_pair_refutes_a_function_of_class_and_displacement {
    // Both rows: class "scooter", displacement_cc 300. Different deposits.
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("xmax-300") == 5000;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("xmax-300-new") == 7000;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("xmax-300-new") != deposit_thb_of_family("xmax-300");
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("xmax-300-new") - deposit_thb_of_family("xmax-300") == 2000;
    assert SCOOTER_300CC_FAMILIES == 3;
    assert SCOOTER_300CC_DISTINCT_DEPOSITS == 2;
}

; ---- what the lookup refuses to answer -------------------------------------------------

test a_tariff_only_key_and_an_unknown_key_are_not_answered_here {
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("pcx-150") == DEPOSIT_NOT_IN_FLEET;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("r7") == DEPOSIT_NOT_IN_FLEET;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("") == DEPOSIT_NOT_IN_FLEET;
    assert DEPOSIT_NOT_IN_FLEET < 0;
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_UNIT_COUNT_IS_DECLARED_HERE == false;
}

; The unit count of the price-list-only families belongs to turbobaby/availability. The edge is the
; owner's ID plus the owner's declaration name, the same shape as MARKET_FX_DECLARATION, and the
; dropped name is listed so a grep for it lands on the resolution rather than on nothing.
test the_price_list_only_unit_count_is_consumed_from_availability {
    assert REUSES_AVAILABILITY_ID == "turbobaby/availability";
    assert REUSES_AVAILABILITY_ID != ID;
    assert AVAILABILITY_UNIT_COUNT_DECLARATION == "PRICE_LIST_ONLY_UNITS";
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_UNIT_COUNT_IS_DECLARED_HERE == false;
    assert RESTATEMENT_DROPPED_ON_RESOLUTION.len == 1;
    assert RESTATEMENT_DROPPED_ON_RESOLUTION[0] == AVAILABILITY_UNIT_COUNT_DECLARATION;
    assert RESTATEMENT_RESOLVED_AT == "2026-09-24";
    assert RESTATEMENT_RESOLVED_AT != MEASURED_AT;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("pcx-150") == DEPOSIT_NOT_IN_FLEET;
    assert deposit_thb_of_family("r7") == DEPOSIT_NOT_IN_FLEET;
}

; Row by row, key beside amount, the way the in-stock table is checked above. Membership in the
; six-tier set is not enough on its own: it holds under any permutation of the seven amounts,
; and a permutation is a wrong published deposit -- pcx-150, the cheapest machine in the tariff
; at 349 THB/day, would carry the R7's 25000 and still pass. These are the seed's
; price_list_only.families rows in seed order.
test the_tariff_only_rows_pin_each_key_to_its_own_published_deposit {
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_KEYS[0] == "pcx-150";
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB[0] == TIER_1_THB;
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_KEYS[1] == "adv-150";
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB[1] == TIER_1_THB;
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_KEYS[2] == "pcx-160";
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB[2] == TIER_2_THB;
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_KEYS[3] == "adv-160";
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB[3] == TIER_2_THB;
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_KEYS[4] == "rebel-300";
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB[4] == TIER_4_THB;
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_KEYS[5] == "xsr-900";
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB[5] == TIER_5_THB;
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_KEYS[6] == "r7";
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB[6] == TIER_6_THB;
    // No tariff-only family sits on the 7000 rung, which is why the set of six is closed over
    // these rows without any of them being the reason a rung exists.
    assert published_rows_at_amount(TIER_3_THB) == TIER_FAMILY_COUNTS[2];
}

test the_tariff_only_deposits_are_all_drawn_from_the_same_six_tiers {
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_KEYS.len == PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB.len;
    assert PRICE_LIST_ONLY_KEYS.len == 7;
    assert is_published_tier(PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB[0]) == true;
    assert is_published_tier(PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB[1]) == true;
    assert is_published_tier(PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB[2]) == true;
    assert is_published_tier(PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB[3]) == true;
    assert is_published_tier(PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB[4]) == true;
    assert is_published_tier(PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB[5]) == true;
    assert is_published_tier(PRICE_LIST_ONLY_DEPOSIT_THB[6]) == true;
}

test zero_is_not_a_tier_and_absent_is_not_zero {
    assert is_published_tier(0) == false;
    assert tier_index_of(0) == TIER_NONE;
    assert DEPOSIT_ABSENT != 0;
    assert DEPOSIT_ABSENT < 0;
    assert DEPOSIT_NOT_IN_FLEET != DEPOSIT_ABSENT;
}

; The header's wiring claim, as literals. It is asserted rather than described because the
; sentence it replaces was false for an unknown length of time and nothing could have caught
; it: a prose absence has no failing state. These three numbers do.
; Corrected 2026-09-22: they do not. Each assert below compares a constant with a literal, so
; only an edit to this file can fail one, and the tree moved from 6 to 19 under them in a day.
; They pin the dated reading in the constants, re-taken on 2026-09-22 (WIRING_REMEASURED_NOTE).
test the_wiring_absence_is_a_measured_number_and_not_a_flat_nothing {
    // Nineteen files outside specs/ name a .t27 or specs/turbobaby, re-measured 2026-09-22.
    // Six on 2026-09-21. The old claim was zero.
    assert WIRING_GREP_HITS == 19;
    // Three of them name this file and all three are gates. One on 2026-09-21.
    assert WIRING_GREP_HITS_NAMING_THIS_FILE == 3;
    assert WIRING_GREP_HITS_NAMING_THIS_FILE < WIRING_GREP_HITS;
    // The claim that actually mattered, and the only one that survived re-measurement:
    // no shipped consumer READS a deposit out of this file. Two gates do, re-measured 2026-09-22.
    assert WIRING_CONSUMERS_OF_THIS_FILE == 0;
}

test the_deposit_is_money_or_the_passport_and_never_both {
    assert deposit_form_is_legal(true, false) == true;
    assert deposit_form_is_legal(false, true) == true;
    assert deposit_form_is_legal(true, true) == false;
    assert deposit_form_is_legal(false, false) == false;
    assert DEPOSIT_FORMS[0] == "money";
    assert DEPOSIT_FORMS[1] == "passport";
}

test no_discount_is_applied_to_a_deposit {
    assert DEPOSIT_DISCOUNT_APPLIES == false;
    assert DEPOSIT_MONEY_METHODS.len == 3;
}

; ---- the refund, and what it refuses ----------------------------------------------------

; The numbering is load-bearing: refund_is_authorized() names two codes, and everything at or
; above REFUND_AUTHORIZED_OUTCOMES must be a refusal. Each of the nine is put through the
; predicate, so a renumbering that moved a refusal below the line fails here.
test the_nine_refund_outcomes_are_two_returns_and_seven_refusals {
    assert REFUND_RETURN_DOCUMENT == 0;
    assert REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD == 1;
    assert REFUND_REFUSED_FORM_ILLEGAL == 2;
    assert REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_UNRECORDED == 3;
    assert REFUND_REFUSED_CURRENCY_UNRECORDED == 4;
    assert REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_UNAGREED == 5;
    assert REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_CHANGED == 6;
    assert REFUND_REFUSED_CURRENCY_CHANGED == 7;
    assert REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_CHANGED == 8;
    assert REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_CHANGED + 1 == REFUND_OUTCOME_COUNT;
    assert REFUND_AUTHORIZED_OUTCOMES == 2;
    assert refund_is_authorized(REFUND_RETURN_DOCUMENT) == true;
    assert refund_is_authorized(REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD) == true;
    assert refund_is_authorized(REFUND_REFUSED_FORM_ILLEGAL) == false;
    assert refund_is_authorized(REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_UNRECORDED) == false;
    assert refund_is_authorized(REFUND_REFUSED_CURRENCY_UNRECORDED) == false;
    assert refund_is_authorized(REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_UNAGREED) == false;
    assert refund_is_authorized(REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_CHANGED) == false;
    assert refund_is_authorized(REFUND_REFUSED_CURRENCY_CHANGED) == false;
    assert refund_is_authorized(REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_CHANGED) == false;
    assert refund_moves_money(REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD) == true;
    assert refund_moves_money(REFUND_RETURN_DOCUMENT) == false;
}

; The method table is the seed's, read through DEPOSIT_MONEY_METHODS: the three money methods
; index, and the two strings that are NOT deposit methods -- the fourth accepted entry, which
; is the passport FORM, and the PromptPay line from payment_methods -- do not.
test the_three_accepted_money_methods_are_the_only_ones_a_refund_can_use {
    assert money_method_index_of(DEPOSIT_MONEY_METHODS[0]) == 0;
    assert money_method_index_of(DEPOSIT_MONEY_METHODS[1]) == 1;
    assert money_method_index_of(DEPOSIT_MONEY_METHODS[2]) == 2;
    assert money_method_index_of("cash THB") == 0;
    assert money_method_index_of("bank transfer") == 1;
    assert money_method_index_of("USDT") == 2;
    assert money_method_index_of(DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED) == MONEY_METHOD_NONE;
    assert money_method_index_of("passport in place of money") == MONEY_METHOD_NONE;
    assert money_method_index_of("Thai PromptPay QR transfer") == MONEY_METHOD_NONE;
}

; Passport in, passport out: the document is handed back and there is no figure to hand back
; with it. The second half is the one that matters -- a request that turns a held passport
; into money is refused, and so is one that turns it into a zero, which D9 forbids reading as
; money in the first place.
test a_passport_deposit_is_returned_as_the_document_and_no_money_moves {
    assert refund_decision(false, true, DEPOSIT_ABSENT, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, DEPOSIT_ABSENT, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED) == REFUND_RETURN_DOCUMENT;
    assert refund_is_authorized(REFUND_RETURN_DOCUMENT) == true;
    assert refund_moves_money(REFUND_RETURN_DOCUMENT) == false;
    assert refund_amount_returned(REFUND_RETURN_DOCUMENT, DEPOSIT_ABSENT) == DEPOSIT_ABSENT;
    assert refund_decision(false, true, DEPOSIT_ABSENT, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, TIER_2_THB, "THB", "cash THB") == REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_CHANGED;
    assert refund_decision(false, true, DEPOSIT_ABSENT, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, TIER_2_THB, "THB", DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED) == REFUND_REFUSED_CURRENCY_CHANGED;
    assert refund_decision(false, true, DEPOSIT_ABSENT, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, TIER_2_THB, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED) == REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_CHANGED;
    assert refund_decision(false, true, DEPOSIT_ABSENT, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, 0, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED) == REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_CHANGED;
}

; Money in, the same money out: the method it arrived by, the currency it was agreed in, the
; figure that was agreed. The third line is the case the tier ladder does not cover -- 6000 is
; an authoritative amount that matches no rung, the one this file already publishes and logs
; rather than snapping -- and the refund follows the AGREED figure, not the ladder.
test money_comes_back_by_the_method_it_arrived_by_at_the_agreed_figure {
    assert refund_decision(true, false, TIER_2_THB, "THB", "bank transfer", TIER_2_THB, "THB", "bank transfer") == REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD;
    assert refund_decision(true, false, TIER_6_THB, "THB", "cash THB", TIER_6_THB, "THB", "cash THB") == REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD;
    assert refund_decision(true, false, 6000, "THB", "USDT", 6000, "THB", "USDT") == REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD;
    assert is_published_tier(6000) == false;
    assert refund_moves_money(REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD) == true;
    assert refund_amount_returned(REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD, TIER_2_THB) == TIER_2_THB;
    assert refund_amount_returned(REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD, 6000) == 6000;
}

; USDT in, cash out is not a refund of this deposit, and neither is the reverse. The method is
; recorded next to the figure (src/db/orders.rs:578-581) for exactly this reason.
test a_changed_method_is_not_a_refund_this_contract_authorizes {
    assert refund_decision(true, false, TIER_2_THB, "THB", "USDT", TIER_2_THB, "THB", "cash THB") == REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_CHANGED;
    assert refund_decision(true, false, TIER_2_THB, "THB", "cash THB", TIER_2_THB, "THB", "bank transfer") == REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_CHANGED;
    assert refund_decision(true, false, TIER_2_THB, "THB", "bank transfer", TIER_2_THB, "THB", DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED) == REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_CHANGED;
    assert refund_is_authorized(REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_CHANGED) == false;
    assert refund_amount_returned(REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_CHANGED, TIER_2_THB) == DEPOSIT_ABSENT;
}

; The FX half of the deferred row, as behaviour: a deposit agreed in baht is not returned in
; dollars, and the request is refused rather than converted. There is no test in the other
; direction -- a deposit agreed in USD, its return requested in THB -- because writing one
; would need a concrete USD figure, and no USD figure can be written in this repository
; without the rate turbobaby/market refuses to publish in EXCHANGE_RATES_PUBLISHED. The
; predicate is symmetric by
; construction: it compares the two currencies and privileges neither.
test a_changed_currency_is_not_a_refund_this_contract_authorizes {
    assert refund_decision(true, false, TIER_4_THB, "THB", "USDT", TIER_4_THB, "USD", "USDT") == REFUND_REFUSED_CURRENCY_CHANGED;
    assert refund_decision(true, false, TIER_4_THB, "THB", "USDT", TIER_4_THB, "EUR", "USDT") == REFUND_REFUSED_CURRENCY_CHANGED;
    assert refund_decision(true, false, TIER_4_THB, "THB", "USDT", TIER_4_THB, CURRENCY, "USDT") == REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD;
    assert CURRENCY == "THB";
    assert refund_is_authorized(REFUND_REFUSED_CURRENCY_CHANGED) == false;
    assert refund_amount_returned(REFUND_REFUSED_CURRENCY_CHANGED, TIER_4_THB) == DEPOSIT_ABSENT;
}

; Any other figure is another transaction. The second and third lines are a part-refund and a
; fee netted off the top; both are refused by the same gate, because this contract has no
; schedule to net anything against -- REFUND_PARTIAL_AMOUNT_ALLOWED and
; REFUND_FEE_SUBTRACTION_ALLOWED say what would be needed. No arithmetic appears in the
; arguments either: the short figures are other published rungs, not a computed shortfall.
test a_changed_amount_is_not_a_refund_this_contract_authorizes {
    assert refund_decision(true, false, TIER_5_THB, "THB", "cash THB", TIER_6_THB, "THB", "cash THB") == REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_CHANGED;
    assert refund_decision(true, false, TIER_5_THB, "THB", "cash THB", TIER_4_THB, "THB", "cash THB") == REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_CHANGED;
    assert refund_decision(true, false, TIER_5_THB, "THB", "bank transfer", TIER_1_THB, "THB", "bank transfer") == REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_CHANGED;
    assert refund_decision(true, false, TIER_5_THB, "THB", "cash THB", 0, "THB", "cash THB") == REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_CHANGED;
    assert refund_is_authorized(REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_CHANGED) == false;
    assert refund_amount_returned(REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_CHANGED, TIER_5_THB) == DEPOSIT_ABSENT;
}

; FAIL CLOSED. In every case here the request matches the record exactly, and every one is
; still refused: an unrecorded method is equal to an unrecorded method, and a rule that
; compared before it checked completeness would hand back money on an empty record. The third
; line is a method the shop takes for RENT but not as a DEPOSIT (data/fleet_seed.json:294
; against :291); the last two are the orders.rs amount None and the zero D9 forbids.
test an_incomplete_deposit_record_fails_closed {
    assert refund_decision(true, false, TIER_2_THB, "THB", DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, TIER_2_THB, "THB", DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED) == REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_UNRECORDED;
    assert refund_decision(true, false, TIER_2_THB, "THB", "passport in place of money", TIER_2_THB, "THB", "passport in place of money") == REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_UNRECORDED;
    assert refund_decision(true, false, TIER_2_THB, "THB", "Thai PromptPay QR transfer", TIER_2_THB, "THB", "Thai PromptPay QR transfer") == REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_UNRECORDED;
    assert refund_decision(true, false, TIER_2_THB, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, "USDT", TIER_2_THB, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, "USDT") == REFUND_REFUSED_CURRENCY_UNRECORDED;
    assert refund_decision(true, false, DEPOSIT_ABSENT, "THB", "USDT", DEPOSIT_ABSENT, "THB", "USDT") == REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_UNAGREED;
    assert refund_decision(true, false, 0, "THB", "USDT", 0, "THB", "USDT") == REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_UNAGREED;
    assert refund_amount_returned(REFUND_REFUSED_METHOD_UNRECORDED, TIER_2_THB) == DEPOSIT_ABSENT;
}

; The form gate runs first, so a record holding both money and the passport -- or neither --
; is refused before any figure is read. deposit_form_is_legal() is the same judge the rest of
; this file uses; the refund does not get a second opinion about what a legal deposit is.
test an_illegal_form_pair_is_refused_before_any_figure_is_read {
    assert deposit_form_is_legal(true, true) == false;
    assert refund_decision(true, true, TIER_2_THB, "THB", "USDT", TIER_2_THB, "THB", "USDT") == REFUND_REFUSED_FORM_ILLEGAL;
    assert deposit_form_is_legal(false, false) == false;
    assert refund_decision(false, false, DEPOSIT_ABSENT, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, DEPOSIT_ABSENT, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED, DEPOSIT_FIELD_UNRECORDED) == REFUND_REFUSED_FORM_ILLEGAL;
    assert refund_is_authorized(REFUND_REFUSED_FORM_ILLEGAL) == false;
}

; The three refusals, and the ownership edge that makes the first of them somebody else's fact
; rather than a second copy of it here. Adding a refund rule added no transaction table: D14
; holds exactly as it did.
test the_refund_rule_converts_nothing_and_nets_nothing_off {
    assert REFUND_FX_CONVERSION_ALLOWED == false;
    assert REFUND_PARTIAL_AMOUNT_ALLOWED == false;
    assert REFUND_FEE_SUBTRACTION_ALLOWED == false;
    assert REUSES_MARKET_PROFILE_ID == "turbobaby/market";
    // The edge is owner plus declaration name, so that it survives an edit to the owner.
    assert MARKET_FX_DECLARATION == "EXCHANGE_RATES_PUBLISHED";
    assert REUSES_MARKET_PROFILE_ID != ID;
    assert PAST_RENTAL_DEPOSITS_THB.len == 0;
    assert refund_amount_returned(REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD, TIER_6_THB) == TIER_6_THB;
    assert refund_amount_returned(REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD, TIER_1_THB) == TIER_1_THB;
    assert refund_amount_returned(REFUND_RETURN_DOCUMENT, TIER_6_THB) == DEPOSIT_ABSENT;
    assert refund_amount_returned(REFUND_REFUSED_AMOUNT_UNAGREED, TIER_6_THB) == DEPOSIT_ABSENT;
}

// ============================================================================
// Invariants
//
// The claims about the whole module that no single example carries: the tier set is closed,
// the family-key domain is total, the tiers do not overlap, the deposit is not a function of
// (class, displacement_cc), the form is exclusive, and no individual rental is published.
// ============================================================================

invariant the_six_tiers_are_the_whole_published_seed_set
  assert TIERS_THB.len == TIER_COUNT

invariant an_unmatched_authoritative_amount_is_not_rewritten_to_a_tier
  assert publishable_deposit(6000) == true and tier_index_of(6000) == TIER_NONE and deposit_needs_tier_log(6000) == true

; TOTALITY, over the family-key domain rather than a displacement band: every offered family
; publishes a deposit, so the lookup never has to invent one for a bike that is for rent.
invariant every_offered_family_has_a_published_tier
  assert FAMILIES_WITH_PUBLISHED_DEPOSIT == TIER_FAMILY_COUNT_SUM

; ...and the domain is closed: the offered families plus the one without a published deposit
; are the whole fleet, so no in-stock family falls outside this spec unnoticed.
invariant the_family_key_domain_is_closed
  assert FAMILIES_WITH_PUBLISHED_DEPOSIT + FAMILIES_WITHOUT_PUBLISHED_DEPOSIT == FAMILY_DEPOSIT_THB.len

; EXACTLY ONE: the per-tier counts add up to the offered count, so the six tiers partition the
; offered families -- none counted twice, none left out.
invariant the_tier_histogram_partitions_the_offered_families
  assert TIER_FAMILY_COUNT_SUM == FAMILIES_WITH_PUBLISHED_DEPOSIT

; ...and the partition is recounted from the family table rather than restated: the six rungs
; between them hold every offered family, counted one row at a time by families_on_tier().
; The published histogram is compared entry by entry in each_rung_is_recounted_from_the_family_table;
; this is the whole-module form of the same claim.
invariant the_rungs_recount_to_the_offered_families
  assert families_on_tier(0) + families_on_tier(1) + families_on_tier(2) + families_on_tier(3) + families_on_tier(4) + families_on_tier(5) == FAMILIES_WITH_PUBLISHED_DEPOSIT

; NON-OVERLAP: the tiers are point values, and the smallest gap between adjacent rungs is
; positive, so the ladder is strictly increasing and no amount can belong to two tiers.
invariant the_tiers_do_not_overlap
  assert TIER_GAP_MIN_THB > 0

; ...and the gaps are the whole ladder, not a subset of it: they sum to the span from the
; lowest tier to the highest, so a rung cannot be dropped without failing here.
invariant the_gap_ladder_spans_the_whole_range
  assert TIER_GAP_SUM_THB == TIER_SPAN_THB

; The refutation of issue #18 as a standing claim rather than a comment: one (class,
; displacement_cc) pair carries more than one deposit, so no function of those two arguments
; can exist, and nobody may add one later without this failing.
invariant deposit_is_not_a_function_of_class_and_displacement
  assert SCOOTER_300CC_DISTINCT_DEPOSITS > 1

; The amount the issue asked for as its top band is published by no row at all. Counted over
; the 21 published rows rather than read off DEPOSIT_10000_OCCURRENCES, which would be the
; constant asserted against its own declaration.
invariant the_ten_thousand_tier_does_not_exist
  assert published_rows_at_amount(10000) == 0

; Money or the passport: two forms, and exactly two legal states of the pair. A third state
; (both) and a fourth (neither) are refused, which is what "never both" means in code.
invariant the_deposit_form_is_exclusive
  assert DEPOSIT_FORM_LEGAL_STATES == DEPOSIT_FORMS.len

; D14: only the aggregate tier is public. The length is the prohibition.
invariant no_individual_rental_deposit_is_published
  assert PAST_RENTAL_DEPOSITS_THB.len == 0

; D9: an absent deposit is a dash, never a zero. A marker below zero cannot be read as money.
invariant the_absent_marker_can_never_be_read_as_money
  assert DEPOSIT_ABSENT < 0

; The refund half of the deferred FX/refund row, as a standing claim: the only outcome that
; moves money hands back the agreed figure unchanged, every other outcome hands back the
; absent marker, a currency change is refused rather than converted, and the three arithmetic
; doors are shut. A conversion, a part-refund or a netted fee would each have to appear as
; arithmetic in refund_amount_returned(), whose body holds one comparison and no arithmetic.
invariant no_refund_path_converts_or_recomputes_an_amount
  assert refund_amount_returned(REFUND_RETURN_SAME_METHOD, TIER_6_THB) == TIER_6_THB and refund_amount_returned(REFUND_RETURN_DOCUMENT, TIER_6_THB) == DEPOSIT_ABSENT and refund_decision(true, false, TIER_2_THB, "THB", "USDT", TIER_2_THB, "USD", "USDT") == REFUND_REFUSED_CURRENCY_CHANGED and REFUND_FX_CONVERSION_ALLOWED == false and REFUND_PARTIAL_AMOUNT_ALLOWED == false and REFUND_FEE_SUBTRACTION_ALLOWED == false
